hello and welcome to the new world  review i'm grand lime waifu and today it  is the day my goodness it's been quite  the journey hasn't it more than a year  and many many many mispronounced and  forgotten names to get us to the point  where i can say we're going to take a  look at the last existing episodes of  hunter hunter episodes 147 and 148 and  see if absolutely everything or  absolutely anything has been resolved  let's get into it episode 147 and i  really like the cyclical nature of some  of tagashi's decisions if anything i  think i'm less interested in whether  everything is resolved and more  interested in what is resolved because  the way tagashi works we can assume i  will assume by now that takashi is  afraid of endings because if you end  things there's no chance of it coming  back if you resolve someone's story what  need do they have to go out into the  world everything related to gone in this  episode was sort of a cleanup for the  first time the boys are choosing to take  time away from each other it's  interesting that earlier in the arc  kilauea said that things would change  once he saved gone because i don't know  if this is what he meant and i don't  know if this is what he expected to  happen the episode was very much about  apologies how to apologize how to atone  koala friend felt that he needed to  atone for the death of the red-haired  woman who occupied that body before kite  we haven't seen koala boy in so long i  did wonder what his deal was but i don't  know if i ever expected this to be  resolved takashi has this really  interesting way of bringing back  characters i sort of forgot to care  about and use them not to move the story  along but to highlight another aspect of  it and make a point i don't care about  the koala's plight at all because i  don't need to i'd argue i'm not supposed  to what i am supposed to do is consider  kite's response to the story which is  somewhat in opposition to what jing told  gone to do when apologizing the  interesting thing with kait's response  to the koala is that kaise is the one  who decided what atonement the koala  would give the koala apologized or  confessed i suppose and did that for his  own reasons but kite then took it way  over the top by saying that you're going  to live forever and apologize forever in  their own way kite became the avenging  angel atonement is very different to  apology and atonement is very different  to behavior change the koala could  apologize every day could do what kite  says every day of his life then still  come back because the change was not  sold deep kite's suggestion that the  koala must now atone is even more odd to  me given the koala felt he was killing  her to free her from a cycle he doesn't  know exists in a strange sort of way  kite's punishing the koala for mercy  then follows up by denying the koala  that same mercy and i guess the value  system is just very strange to me  especially when we follow it up with  gone and kite's conversation we see such  a powerful difference between the two  gone apologizes and it seems to be only  because kite themself also needs to  atone for something putting gone into a  situation he wasn't ready for and that  allows for that distinct difference in  behavior how kite has become the judge  and jury i'm not sure but i suppose if  you have a lot of people coming to you  to apologize for not doing more you get  that privilege i guess meanwhile i loved  that killer didn't let gon drop his  apology he mocked him soundly for it  first jokes are interesting things  because when we joke there's a kernel of  belief at the center of it a kernel that  we have to accept as part of it for it  to be funny the colonel at the center of  kiehl's joke with gone is that he was  left hurt and gone has to accept and  live with that in order to laugh or move  past it that does indicate they can move  past it and be friends and i really like  that and it's really important because  by the time we get to this penultimate  episode kiawah's finally figured out  what he wants to do both of these kids  have had a very specific goal to their  journeys gone wanted to find his father  while kiwa wanted to figure out what he  wants to do with his time what he wants  to do with his life at many points  throughout the series kilwa has  very specifically been following gone  because he didn't know what else to be  doing with his time now he has alaka and  something to take care of he's found his  purpose or at least until alaka loans  him to gone because that was an amazing  moment alec is setting them up for a  date even alaka sees the situation for  what it is killer can't follow gone like  a puppy anymore because he knows what he  needs and what he wants isn't purely  gone related anymore and that's some  beautiful growth you know and gone well  gone managed to find his dad and this is  what i meant about the cyclical nature  of things episode 1 we were in a tree  with gone here at the end we're in a  tree with him and his dad gone was  always on an adventure to find his dad  but more than that he was on a journey  to understand why his dad enjoyed  hunting having accidentally stumbled  across his dad while lying in a  mummified state did he learn that i'm  hoping that's one of the answered  questions so let's take a look at the  final episode so the final episode of  hunter hunter if there is any more to  this show i don't think it will fit as  well as what we got i mean all the  flashbacks and the climbing and the  wonder of the size of the tree truly did  make for a nice jumping off point as it  were and i really love what jing had to  say to gone about why he left he had a  reason a strong reason not only did he  have a reason but he had learning to  pass on experiences he's had have been  paralleled to gons surprisingly closely  but i don't think gone could have  understood them or truly come to terms  with the meanings of them without jinx  wrapping up of those experiences it  continues that cyclical nature of things  knowing that jing had to learn how to  appreciate the happiness of those around  him there are distinct differences  between jing and gon and i think one of  them is the interaction with the world  jing left because he was curious as did  gone but where one was curious about  what he hadn't seen the other was  curious about what he hadn't seen jing  left because he wanted to know what was  out there gone left because he wanted to  know what jing wanted now that he knows  what jing wants and how his father  relates to the world i imagine he can  understand where he wants to go from  here but really if you look at the  conversation they had gone is now in the  same position keowa was in when he  decided to follow gone kilwa went with  gon because he didn't know what he  wanted gon now gets to spend some time  figuring out what that is the trope of  the real treasure being the friends we  find along the way is a nice way to end  a series based around a character i've  repeatedly questioned as not being able  to empathize with others there's  something magical about the entire  journey existing in order for him to  learn how to empathize in just enough  time for him to meet his dad who seems  to be stacked so full of empathy that  his original goal was superseded in  happiness by the happiness on others  faces i also loved that jinx's game was  a metaverse version of what he knew his  world was a smaller subset of a broader  world i'm entertained by the way that  was represented artistically and there  were so many odd perspectives in that  one image of the world the big world the  extra world outside the world you know  yeah i'm not sure what to believe other  than that is jing's internal  representation of what the world might  look like and i almost understand now  why the hunter exam exists we got there  there are people out there who  understand that the world is bigger and  broader and more dangerous than anyone  could possibly realize but it takes  those four elements to be able to take  them on especially since going into the  world could result in someone or  something following you back if you  return which leads me to wonder whether  the queen ant floated in from outside  the humanish world or if she was tempted  in she suggested at one point that maybe  she had some human in her and if she  came from another world it would make  sense that humans in fact created the  issue they then had to resolve right  because that's that is what humans do  monsters those four aspects really  resonated with me authorization means  there's a group that know about it means  says there's a correct way to do it  qualification and the fact that he  doesn't have it suggest that even jing  has a long way to go to be able to  survive that broader world and a  contract that suggests people might want  it explored jing knows something about  all of them he's worked too hard not to  know anything about any of them but he  doesn't tell gone because that's part of  the game ultimately the sharing of  stories between them shows that gone has  been accepted by his father so jin can  only say that his son found him despite  his best wishes and despite the fact  that he kind of accidentally stumbled  across him you know that doesn't matter  good job as they laughed i did kind of  think of that point and thought i'd be a  really dick move if he went  zoom and disappeared again because being  found is his way of showing appreciation  for another hunter the outro of the  final episode made it though right it  made the entire episode seeing everyone  becoming who they were supposed to  become having those couple of  resolutions you know it was enough i  wish milky moomoo's hawk had shown up  but otherwise i really enjoyed what we  got kurapika and his eye collection was  a clear favorite for me i'm somewhat  surprised and sad we didn't get a final  shot of hiskey but maybe that's to be  expected i'd have liked to know where he  ended up but unsatisfied is probably the  the fact of the matter isn't it really  leorio in what we assume is a consulting  doctor's office or at least rich which  is exactly what he wanted and you know  he deserves it ultimately the only  important character that died in the  entire series being natero i mean other  than uh the the the ants the ant king  and his queen which was a beautiful  thing for us to see just saying but  beyond those two dying the only  important character that died in the  series was the tarot and that was  poignant and pointed and i really love  that someone with such a zest for life  gave his up to make sure the rest of  them could continue to bumble their way  through between the first arc where he  spent his time playing with the boys to  learn their potential to the point where  we saw his gratitude for existence to  his willingness to give himself over to  the world with that gratitude there have  been a lot of really interesting  messages that came from the series the  idea that there's nothing to distinguish  human from monster and that even if we  think we know we really don't the idea  that sometimes the best revenge is  revenge we refuse to take the idea that  there's no point in being the best if  there is no one at the top for you to  play with the idea that all the power in  the world won't win you the game the  idea that the pleasure we see on the  faces of others can be its own reward  and the idea that maybe sometimes the  detours are what make the journey worth  taking this series was one hell of a  detour for me and one that overall i  quite enjoyed so all i can say is enjoy  the little detours to the fullest even  if they're 148 episodes long stay  hydrated enjoy some fresh air and maybe  i'll see you next time

